      "content": "To address this concern, consider using geographically weighted regression (GWR) or spatial interpolation methods like kriging, which allow spatial indicators to be localized to specific neighborhoods, minimizing impact on individual-level credit scores. Additionally, incorporating robust regressioning or using regularization techniques like L1 or L2 norm minimizing the effect of extreme z-score values can help prevent artifacts from spatial features. By normalizing or scaling the spatial indicators, you can reduce the impact of external influences and prevent modeling biases towards specific demographics.",
